{# A portal's own accent colour, overriding the `:root` value from style.css.

   It is emitted here rather than in `base.html.twig` because **there is no one
   layout**: 23 templates extend `base`, the admin screens carry their own
   `<head>`, and this partial is the one thing every page with site chrome
   includes. A `<style>` outside `<head>` is tolerated everywhere and is the
   honest trade for that; it stops being needed the day a single layout exists.

   Nothing is emitted at all when the portal overrides nothing, so the default
   site keeps rendering byte-identical markup. #}
{# 🔴 **Les préréglages (S166) sortent AVANT la couleur, et séparément.** Ils
   n'ont pas la même condition : un labo peut choisir une densité sans changer sa
   couleur, et l'inverse. Les mêler dans un seul `{% if %}` aurait fait dépendre
   l'un de l'autre.
   ⚠️ Chaîne vide au préréglage livré ⇒ aucune balise émise, balisage identique au
   bit près.

   ⚠️ **`|raw` est correct ICI** : la chaîne est fabriquée par `ThemePresets` à
   partir d'entiers calculés et de noms de jetons écrits en dur. Aucune saisie
   d'exploitant n'y entre — les trois axes sont des listes FERMÉES, vérifiées au
   point de passage. Sans `raw`, les accolades sortiraient échappées et la règle
   ne s'appliquerait pas. #}
{% set preset_css = theme_preset_css() %}
{% if preset_css %}<style>{{ preset_css|raw }}</style>{% endif %}

{% set portal_color = portal_primary_color() %}
{% if portal_color %}
    {# 🔴 **`--color-primary-text` est émis AUSSI, et calculé en PHP (S166b/S167).**
       `style.css` le dérive en thème sombre avec `color-mix()` et garde un repli
       statique — or un repli statique ne peut pas suivre un thème : sur un moteur
       sans `color-mix()`, un labo qui change sa couleur gardait l'accent de
       FabOS. Calculé ici, il suit la palette partout, et l'aperçu montre la même
       chose que la publication.
       ⚠️ En thème CLAIR le jeton vaut la couleur elle-même ; ce n'est qu'en
       sombre qu'il s'éclaircit, d'où les deux règles. #}
    <style>:root { --color-primary: {{ portal_color }}; --border-color-primary: {{ portal_color }}; --color-primary-text: {{ portal_color }}; }
    {%- set portal_text = portal_primary_text() -%}
    {%- if portal_text %} html[data-theme="dark"] { --color-primary-text: {{ portal_text }}; }{% endif %}</style>
{% endif %}

<div class="alert-bar">
    {% include 'site/_alert_bar.html.twig' %}
</div>

<header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-container">
        <a href="{{ path('app_home') }}" class="header-brand">
            <div class="logo-ensea">
                {% include 'site/_logo.html.twig' %}
            </div>
        </a>

        <nav class="main-navbar">
            <div class="navbar-container">
                {# Assembled by NavBuilder from what is switched on. A group with no
                   visible children never reaches here, so no empty dropdown can render;
                   and hiding an entry only hides a link — the route gate and the
                   firewall are what decide whether a page exists. #}
                {#
                   ⚠️ The active state is computed by `nav_is_current()` (path
                   prefix, so a detail page still lights its section) and never
                   here. A template that decides which entry is current is a
                   template every other nav surface has to copy — the footer and
                   the error page render the same entries.

                   `aria-current="page"` and not only a class: the class is what
                   you see, the attribute is what a screen reader announces, and
                   a menu that looks like it says where you are while saying
                   nothing to assistive tech is worse than one that says nothing
                   to anybody.
                #}
                {% for entry in nav_header() %}
                    {% set label = entry.translate ? entry.label|trans : entry.label %}
                    {% if entry.kind == 'group' %}
                        {# A group is current when any of its children is — otherwise
                           "Apprendre" goes dark the moment you open a training, which
                           is exactly when it should be lit. #}
                        {% set here = nav_is_current(entry.route, entry.params)
                            or entry.items|filter(item => nav_is_current(item.route, item.params))|length > 0 %}
                        <div class="navbar-item navbar-has-dropdown">
                            <a href="{{ path(entry.route, entry.params) }}"
                               class="navbar-link{{ here ? ' active' : '' }}"
                               {% if here %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>{{ label }}</a>
                            <div class="navbar-dropdown">
                                {% for item in entry.items %}
                                    {% set item_here = nav_is_current(item.route, item.params) %}
                                    <a href="{{ path(item.route, item.params) }}"
                                       class="navbar-dropdown-link{{ item.child ? ' navbar-dropdown-child' : '' }}{{ item_here ? ' active' : '' }}"
                                       {% if item_here %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.translate ? item.label|trans : item.label }}</a>
                                {% endfor %}
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    {% else %}
                        {% set here = nav_is_current(entry.route, entry.params) %}
                        <a href="{{ path(entry.route, entry.params) }}"
                           class="navbar-link{{ here ? ' active' : '' }}"
                           {% if here %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ label }}</a>
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </nav>

        <div class="header-right">
            {#
               🔴 This was a bare <input> and <button> with **no form**, made to
               work by a click handler in `main.js` that set
               `window.location.href = '/search?q=…'` — a hardcoded path, not
               `path()`. So it did nothing at all before that script loaded, and
               nothing ever without JS: a control that looks like it works and
               does not, which is exactly what the no-dead-affordances rule is
               about. It is now an ordinary GET form. It works with the script
               deleted, it works before the script arrives, and Enter submits it
               because that is what Enter does in a form.

               ⚠️ `name="q"` matches what `app_recherche` reads, and the action goes
               through `path()` so a sub-directory deployment or a renamed route
               follows it.

               ⚠️ Was `app_search` — `/search`, an English-path duplicate of the
               same page. Deleted with the rest of the legacy routes (operator,
               2026-08-16: "pre V1 dev site, no need to retain legacy anything").
            #}
            {# S194 — « / » place le curseur ici, depuis n'importe quelle page. #}
            <form class="header-search" action="{{ path('app_recherche') }}" method="get" role="search" data-controller="search-shortcut">
                <input type="search" name="q" value="{{ app.request.query.get('q')|default('') }}" data-search-shortcut-target="input" aria-keyshortcuts="/"
                       placeholder="{{ 'common.search_placeholder'|trans }}" class="search-input-header"
                       aria-label="{{ 'common.search'|trans }}">
                <button type="submit" class="search-button-header" aria-label="{{ 'common.search'|trans }}">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/>
                        <path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
            </form>
            <div class="header-auth">
                {% include 'site/_header_auth.html.twig' %}
            </div>
            <button class="mobile-nav-toggle" aria-label="Menu">
                <span></span>
                <span></span>
                <span></span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>
